<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16040" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĕpŭlāris</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		epulum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a
			banquet.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">epularis accubitio amicorum,</span>”
				<i>at a banquet</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Sen. 13 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sacrificium ludorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. de
					Or. 3, 19 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">1. epulo, II.: sermo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 2, p. 123</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: EPULARES appellabantur, qui in
			quibusdam ludis nocte epulabantur, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest.
				p. 82, 10</span></i> Müll.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
